# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Never commit .env.local.
#
# The Supabase SERVICE-ROLE key is deliberately absent from this file. It is set
# in Vercel server environment variables only, is used by exactly one code path
# (account deletion), and must never appear in a local file or in git history.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# Waitlist uses the existing Supabase URL and public key above. Apply
# supabase/migrations/0002_waitlist.sql to the same project; no webhook required.

# Launch gate (proxy.ts). Unset/anything but "true" -- the default in every
# environment, including production -- means only the coming-soon page and
# /api/waitlist are public; every other route 404s. Set to "true" in Vercel
# once the real app is ready to go public.
# APP_LAUNCHED=

# --- Session 17A: standalone PostHog project (US cloud; EU was recommended for
# this health-data app but Rochak chose to stay on US for now, 2026-09-12). ---
# Session replay is confirmed enabled with full input and text masking.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=

# --- RLS test suite only (tests/rls/), read from .env.local same as everything
# above. Same project as NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL/ANON_KEY, just without the
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix — plus the service-role key, which must NEVER get a
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix or ship to the client. Used only by `npm run test`
# locally; the app itself never reads these three.
# SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
